Also, it is not possible to check the assertions for lines where comments start with "@@@", as these comments are not always immediately associated with specific code. However, you should note that assertions in Python are used for debugging purposes and should not be used as replacement for proper code logic, as they can be disabled using the `-O` option in command lines. As a best practice, use assertions sparingly to check for basic assumptions in your code. For more complex requirements, consider using other forms of input validation or error handling in your code.
